<title>FRANCE: Danone denies market talk of asset sale.</title>
<headline>Danone denies market talk of asset sale.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-01-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>French food group Danone denied on Wednesday market rumours that it was set to sell its bottling or beer activities.</p>
<p>Market sources said the rumour had been running in the market and may have caused a rise in Danone shares. The stock was up 0.74 percent at 817 francs, on volume of 357,475 shares at 1500 GMT, while the market was down 1.08 percent.</p>
<p>Another possible reason for the rise was talk the company would post 1996 sales higher than expected after today's close, the sources said.</p>
</text>
